WEBVTT

00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:06.600
Hey, are you sure we should be

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.860
attending the wedding ceremony with you?

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:17.580
Capital
Stuttburg

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.710
Brother Erich said I should 
bring my friends if I had any.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.900
Though I'm just glad the academy 
is out for summer break right now.

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:16.600
Ta-da!

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.100
When I show up in this dress that I picked out,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:24.540
I'm sure all the nobles will want to employ me!

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:27.120
Because it's so showy!

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.250
Are there any nobles coming 
to your brother's wedding?

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:33.970
Hey.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:37.320
He's marrying into the Brandt family, 
which I've heard is a knightdom,

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.680
so yeah, there should be at least some.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.140
Onward I go on the path 
to becoming a retainer!

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:49.910
Oh, sorry...

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:50.690
Huh?

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:52.490
Er?

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.710
I don't trust it.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:57.850
A ship flying in the sky?

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.080
Don't worry, little Er.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:10.040
A magic airship won't fall out of the sky.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.730
I thought only your friends 
were invited to come?

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:18.820
Yeah, Brantag is heading to the capital 
to report the status of his domain,

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:21.260
so he's just guiding us 
since it's on the way for him.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:21.970
Oh?

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.310
Is that a guidebook for the capital?

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.440
Yeah. To be honest, there's something
 I've always wanted.

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:34.320
I see... It won't fall out of the sky, huh?

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.780
Well, I wouldn't say it's impossible.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.550
I mean, if it gets attacked 
by a huge dragon,

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.340
it's bound to fall, y'know?

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.560
True, it would probably fall in that case.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:28.170
The 8th Son?
 Are You Kidding Me?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:34.480
Episode 4: 
Obligations? Are You Kidding Me?!

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.060
Hey, what's going on?!

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.900
I thought this magic airship's flight path 
was avoiding the lands where monsters live?

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:40.560
Yes, but what you see outside right now is 
an undead version of an ancient dragon,

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.860
so that logic doesn't apply here.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:44.870
Enough excuses! Just do something about it!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:45.800
Do want us to die?!

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.060
Everyone, please rest easy!

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:55.000
The powerful mage, Brantag Ringstat, 
will be dealing with it right away!

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.420
I can't beat that thing.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:01.570
What?!

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:03.240
That's an undead.

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:06.390
The only way to defeat it is 
by purging it with holy magic.

00:04:06.740 --> 00:04:09.370
But I can't use holy magic.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.810
Then this ship is...

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:16.270
Don't worry. You have another mage on board.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.780
Huh?! Wait, I can't do it!

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:23.700
I mean, th-th-that's—

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:28.160
Your master would have taken 
care of it with a smile.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.620
Listen up. I'll protect the ship.

00:04:34.890 --> 00:04:36.900
The moment you leap off and take flight,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.710
waste no time purging it
with your holy magic.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:42.700
Okay, boy, brace yourself.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.490
Here we go.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.990
Oh, wait a second.

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.770
One more thing.

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:09.370
A magic barrier!

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.330
I told you I'd protect it, didn't I,
 my disciple's disciple?

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:15.710
I should have expected that 
from my master's master.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:16.290
Now...

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.210
I can focus on this moving puppet.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.020
That's it, Well!

00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:38.020
You've got it!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:38.680
Don't lose!

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.190
Settle down, you three. It's dangerous!

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:49.760
I need more.

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:51.840
More, more...

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.960
Even brighter holy light!

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.920
Now, I hope this...

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.470
finishes it!

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.390
Go!

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:17.390
Hey, you three!

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:53.640
Yeah!

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:58.070
Hey, boy!

00:06:58.070 --> 00:07:01.560
I told you to use your bag 
to collect those bones!

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:06.760
Huh?

00:07:07.180 --> 00:07:08.440
Oh, shoot.

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:36.430
Cheers!

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:43.570
Looks like we'll make it to the capital safely.

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:44.970
I'm glad.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.840
I've been wanting to do some shopping.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:49.490
It might prove difficult to go shopping.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:53.220
Hey, Aruterio. You were aboard this ship, too?

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:56.970
Yeah. I enjoyed watching from 
afar as you defeated that dragon.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.290
Sheesh...

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:02.360
Oh, this is one of my partners from 
back when I was still an adventurer.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:04.940
Huh? You were members of the same party?

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:08.690
He's the head of a huge merchant 
company in the capital now.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:11.610
He's known for his business's political ties.

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:15.910
That's about the gist of it. 
Nice to meet you, little hero.

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:17.680
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.770
So what did you mean about
 shopping being difficult?

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:24.350
Oh, well, you'll understand 
once we're in the capital.

00:08:42.730 --> 00:08:44.670
Oh, look at that!

00:08:47.870 --> 00:08:50.140
That's the capital,

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.000
Stuttburg.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:02.930
Hey, why don't we go enjoy 
the town for a bit first?

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.140
Good idea!

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.250
I might want to buy one 
of the capital's dresses!

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:09.270
Uh, well, I have some things to attend to,

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.840
so please take care of the rest.
 All of it. Everything.

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.640
He escaped.

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:19.790
Escaped?

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:25.660
Huh? What?

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.620
Did we do something wrong?

00:09:34.590 --> 00:09:38.220
You did a splendid job of
slaying that ancient dragon.

00:09:41.400 --> 00:09:43.340
His Majesty awaits you at the castle.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.060
Please come this way.

00:09:49.850 --> 00:09:50.730
His Majesty?

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.800
<i>This place is huge...</i>

00:09:57.810 --> 00:09:59.010
Well!

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:02.710
We'll be heading to your brother's, okay?

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:04.250
Bye-bye!

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.690
Huh?!

00:10:06.690 --> 00:10:08.800
Hey, boy, you'll get lost.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:11.880
Oh, p-please wait for me!

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:22.580
The slayer of the ancient dragon, 
Wendelin von Benno Baumeister,

00:10:22.580 --> 00:10:25.250
and standing in for Brantag Ringstat,

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:28.980
Aruterio Märchen, have both arrived!

00:10:44.030 --> 00:10:45.970
Raise your heads.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.560
You truly are young...

00:11:03.650 --> 00:11:07.000
Wendelin von Benno Baumeister.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:07.470
Yes?

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:10.310
In honor of your achievements

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:15.360
in slaying an ancient dragon and defending the 
lives of the passengers on our magic airship,

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:20.260
I hereby grant thee the sixth rank of baronet.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.850
Hey, remember what I taught
 you earlier? Your pledge.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.460
My sword shall be wielded for Your Majesty,

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:34.850
for our kingdom,

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.800
and for our people.

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:43.280
<i>Huh? Did I just become a baronet?</i>

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:47.950
In addition, we hereby bestow 
upon you the twin dragon medal.

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:53.600
Are you sure it was okay 
to miss seeing His Majesty?

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.770
It's fine.

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:57.120
The boy is the star of the show, anyway.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.570
Oh, thank you.

00:11:58.570 --> 00:12:02.280
Um, is Well really going to become a baronet?

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.490
Oh, I'm sure he'll earn a 
noble rank at least that high.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.550
I can't believe he'd be 
granted a higher noble rank

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:11.460
than our father on his journey 
to my wedding ceremony.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:15.650
Oh, yeah, your family only had 
the rank of knight, didn't they?

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:19.090
Um, if he really is being made a baronet,

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:22.360
wouldn't that create a 
separate, independent line?

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:25.420
Yeah, it means his name will be 
removed from your family line

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.560
and placed at the head of 
a new Baumeister family.

00:12:30.480 --> 00:12:34.440
Is Well going to stop being 
an adventurer and leave us?

00:12:35.170 --> 00:12:37.380
No, no, even if he is granted nobility,

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.020
he's just a noble of the robe,
 one without any land.

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:42.600
He won't have any reason to stay in the capital,

00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:46.110
so whether or not he goes adventuring 
should be entirely up to him.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:50.430
Yeah, this is an exciting promotion for Well!

00:12:52.100 --> 00:12:55.540
There are some exciting aspects to it, but...

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:56.670
But?

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.210
Well, I'm sure our boy is getting a full taste

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:05.660
of the fetters that come with noble society.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:12.410
170,000 gold coins for the 
bones and magic stones?

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:16.620
Lord Marshall Edgar, I believe 
130,000 coins is the fair amount.

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:19.800
So he told me to collect them 
because they go for a high price.

00:13:20.130 --> 00:13:22.590
Lord Commissioner Ruckner,

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:25.900
are you suggesting we should be stingy 
with the reward for Sir Baumeister

00:13:25.900 --> 00:13:27.820
after he risked his life in battle?

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.830
Oh, but I didn't really—

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.060
We do not have an unlimited budget.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.870
Sir Baumeister is already 
a citizen of this kingdom,

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:36.440
so I'm sure he understands the circumstances.

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:37.540
Um...

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:40.660
With the bones of this ancient 
dragon and the magic crystals

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.560
we could create from such a huge magic stone,

00:13:42.560 --> 00:13:46.530
we could make several of our 
magic airships operational again!

00:13:46.530 --> 00:13:51.310
Sir Baumeister had the foresight to see that,
 and you intend to waste his efforts?

00:13:51.310 --> 00:13:52.120
Uh, I just—

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:55.030
We're discussing priorities right now.

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:58.560
I'm sure Sir Baumeister 
already understands that!

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:03.360
I think both of you need to calm down a bit.

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:06.630
Each of you makes a good point.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:10.500
So why not compromise and 
provide 150,000 gold coins?

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:14.450
Cardinal Hohenheim, 
this is not such a simple matter.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.370
With all due respect,

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:21.450
Sir Baumeister is the center of attention 
here in the capital right now,

00:14:21.450 --> 00:14:24.840
as the believer of the light 
who defeated that bone dragon.

00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:30.000
I do not believe it would be 
prudent for the royal family

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.220
to embarrass themselves before 
Sir Baumeister any further.

00:14:37.390 --> 00:14:40.620
Forgive my intrusion. I simply 
couldn't bear to watch them

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:43.580
waste any more of your 
precious time, Sir Baumeister.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:44.880
Oh, I was just—

00:14:44.200 --> 00:14:47.180
Now, let us begin making the arrangements.

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.840
Looks like we have Cardinal 
Hohenheim trying to

00:14:54.840 --> 00:14:57.640
curry favor with you, to bring you 
under the church's influence,

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.890
while Lord Marshall Edgar is hoping to use 
you in his efforts to strengthen the military.

00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:07.130
Meanwhile, Lord Commissioner Ruckner is just 
focused on reducing the money they spend on you.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.560
Sir Baumeister!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:19.780
Please behold this!

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.810
My secret technique: Spinning Spear!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.030
Is that some kind of street performer?

00:15:29.030 --> 00:15:32.640
No, that's someone hoping 
you'll hire them as a retainer.

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:33.980
Huh? Me?!

00:15:33.980 --> 00:15:35.360
Of course.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.550
You're a noble with a promising future,

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:41.730
who just received the twin dragon medal that 
no one has earned in over two centuries.

00:15:41.730 --> 00:15:45.760
What do you say?! I'm confident that I'm 
second to none when it comes to the spear!

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:46.940
What do you think you're doing?!

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.630
My name is—

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.630
Stop! Stop!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.510
Do that in your own home!

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:50.510
W-Wait just a...

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.840
You're going to be swamped 
with hopefuls like that,

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:58.790
along with rich merchants begging 
you to wed their daughters.

00:15:58.790 --> 00:16:00.640
I'm going to be swamped with this stuff?

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:05.870
You probably won't be able to 
set foot outside for a while.

00:16:05.870 --> 00:16:08.550
Huh? Then when am I supposed to go shopping?!

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:11.570
That's why I said it might be difficult.

00:16:13.470 --> 00:16:17.430
It's the price of fame you pay 
for being a proper noble.

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:19.500
This is so inconvenient...

00:16:30.720 --> 00:16:32.300
It's been a long time.

00:16:32.980 --> 00:16:34.640
Hey, Well.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:35.760
How have you been?

00:16:36.270 --> 00:16:38.970
You guys don't seem very happy.

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:43.440
The truth is, we haven't received the 
wedding gift from our family yet.

00:16:47.170 --> 00:16:50.840
That's bad... isn't it?

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:52.480
Of course it's bad.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:58.410
Everyone attending will think the groom's 
family is a bunch of crass, rude nobles.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.790
Worse yet, I just got a letter 
from our brother, Kurt...

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.870
Though I'm sure the one who 
actually wrote it was Amalie.

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:07.490
Anyway, to sum it up,

00:17:07.490 --> 00:17:11.930
it said they don't have the money, so he's 
asking me and Paul to pay it for them.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:16.290
What does he think two guards like us can do?

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:19.800
Does he have any idea how 
humbly we have to live?

00:17:20.090 --> 00:17:22.770
Then what about getting them flowers?

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:27.810
Well, a wedding gift is also 
a symbol of noble status.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:30.250
So it has to be something 
gaudy and extravagant.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.370
Status, huh?

00:17:32.370 --> 00:17:38.190
But doesn't this also mean they'll be 
shaming the Duke of Bleichröder, too?

00:17:38.190 --> 00:17:40.200
Huh? Why would it go that far?

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.160
Because, Well,

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:48.660
the Baumeister family are 
vassals of the Duke of Bleichröder.

