00:18:00.690 --> 00:18:04.410
So as it is now, it will look 
like Duke Bleichröder

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:07.030
refused to lend us the money.

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:10.000
Though, of course, it's our family's fault for

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:12.750
not asking the duke to lend 
it in the first place.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:15.110
We probably didn't ask because 
we have no way to repay it.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.890
Um, should I go ahead and pay for it?

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:28.110
Congratulations on your wedding!

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:32.210
Baumeister
Family

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:38.170
<i>Being a noble is such a pain.</i>

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.430
Hey, you don't look too 
thrilled there, nobleman.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:49.560
Keep sighing, and all 
your happiness will escape.

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:51.920
Hey, Aruterio.

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:53.440
Man, I had to hunt this down.

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:55.490
We weren't carrying it at any of our shops,

00:18:55.490 --> 00:18:57.700
so I had to ask a trader I know for it.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.130
Huh? You mean...

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.030
You found it for me?!

00:19:01.260 --> 00:19:04.010
Apparently he obtained it 
from Mizuho in the north.

00:19:04.010 --> 00:19:07.880
Just what is this "kome-kouji," anyway?

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.420
Hey, are you trying to start 
some kind of business?

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:16.640
If you are, could you let me know first?

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:26.330
What's going on all of a sudden?

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:30.610
Brantag said he was going to 
show us the capital's nightlife.

00:19:30.610 --> 00:19:31.740
Just come with me!

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:33.270
Come on! We're home!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.680
Whoa... Hang on!

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.180
Quit pulling!

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:36.240
Just come on! Hurry!

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:36.240
Wait, I said!

