00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:02.860
You were trying this back home, right?

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:04.840
Making "miso," you called it?

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:08.150
Yeah, but I couldn't get it to ferment well.

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:10.110
It always ended up rotting.

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:13.310
I figured it would be difficult 
without kome-kouji.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.510
Hup...

00:20:29.870 --> 00:20:33.860
There. Normally, we would now 
let this rest for a whole year...

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.460
But I'll use magic.

00:20:43.650 --> 00:20:46.460
Please, ferment correctly this time!

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.000
<i>Now that I think about it,</i>

00:20:52.000 --> 00:20:54.520
<i>I once spoke to an artisan who made miso</i>

00:20:54.880 --> 00:20:57.580
<i>back when I was still an employee 
at a trading company.</i>

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.360
<i>He asked me if I knew the difference 
between fermentation and rot.</i>

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:09.240
<i>If I remember right, the correct answer 
was that they're both the same process,</i>

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:12.640
<i>but it's fermentation 
when it's useful to people,</i>

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:15.690
<i>and it's rot when it's harmful.</i>

00:21:18.890 --> 00:21:21.100
<i>Maybe it's the same with being a noble.</i>

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:25.770
<i>It brings a lot of trouble with it,</i>

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:31.620
<i>but I have to live in this 
world regardless, so...</i>

00:21:33.700 --> 00:21:35.000
It's delicious!

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:39.140
<i>I think it's better if I live intelligently,</i>

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.360
<i>and get others to believe 
I'm the fermenting kind of noble.</i>

00:21:54.550 --> 00:21:56.820
You summoned me, Grandfather?

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:59.150
Oh, you're here.

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:07.990
Elise, I've decided who your husband will be.
